const faq: [string, string][] = [
  ['Is cold email legal?', 'In most markets, B2B cold email is legal when you follow the local rules. In the US, the CAN-SPAM Act requires an accurate sender, honest subject lines, a working way to opt out that you honor within 10 business days, and a valid postal address. In the UK and EU, B2B outreach usually relies on legitimate interest and still needs a clear opt-out. Check the rules for each country you email.'],
  ['How many cold emails can I send per day?', 'Fewer than most people think. Spread sending across several mailboxes on separate domains, start low while mailboxes warm up, and increase only while replies stay healthy and complaints stay near zero. Volume is the main reason outreach domains get burned.'],
  ['What is a good reply rate for cold email?', 'It varies widely by market, offer and list quality, so treat any single benchmark with care. The more useful test is your own trend: if replies and booked meetings per 100 people contacted rise as you sharpen the list and message, the program is working.'],
  ['Should I use my main domain for cold email?', 'No. Send outreach from separate domains that look like your brand, so a reputation problem never reaches the domain your invoices, support and customer emails come from.'],
  ['How many follow ups should a cold email sequence have?', 'Two or three follow ups after the first email is a sensible default, spaced a few days apart. Each one should add something new: a proof point, a short resource or a simpler question. Stop as soon as someone replies or asks you to.'],
];
