  </Info>
  <p>Read the full stories: <a href="/case-studies/scalability/">Scalability</a>, <a href="/case-studies/maestro/">Maestro</a> and <a href="/case-studies/soulful-evolution/">Soulful Evolution</a>.</p>

  <h2>What does a 2026 outreach system look like?</h2>
  <p>A working outreach system in 2026 is a small pipeline with clear steps, where people make the judgment calls and software does the repeat work.</p>

  <Info eyebrow="The system" title="From buyer profile to booked meeting" theme="light">
    <Flow steps={[
      { t: 'Define the buyer', p: 'Role, company type and the trigger that makes now a good time.' },
      { t: 'Research and verify', p: 'Build a small list, check every address, note one reason per person.' },
      { t: 'Send from clean domains', p: 'Authenticated, warmed mailboxes at low daily volume.' },
      { t: 'Follow up with value', p: 'Two or three steps, plus LinkedIn for the same people.' },
      { t: 'Hand off and measure', p: 'Replies reach sales fast. Track meetings and revenue, not opens.' },
    ]} />
  </Info>

  <p>AI now helps with the research and first drafts, which makes careful personalization affordable at a sensible scale. It does not replace judgment about who to contact or what is worth saying. We cover where that line sits in <a href="/learn/what-are-ai-agents/">our guide to AI agents</a>.</p>

